# What is product, and what is repository furniture.
#
# bin/build-dist.sh and the release workflow both read this file, so it is the
# only place the answer is written down. Everything listed here serves the
# repository — versioning it, building it, or explaining it — and would be
# noise in a site owner's wp-content/plugins directory.

# Version control and repository configuration.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.distignore

# Release tooling. The plugin is built by these; it does not contain them.
.github
bin
build
*.zip

# Repository-facing. It routes people to the issue tracker and the docs, which
# is a repository's job; readme.txt already carries what WordPress shows a site
# owner inside wp-admin.
SUPPORT.md

# Not tracked in this repository, and listed anyway. Development happens in
# shubochandrosarker/memberistic, and a maintainer packaging a build from a
# working copy that has a vendor/ or a test cache lying around should get the
# same archive as the release runner — not one with a Composer tree inside it.
vendor
node_modules
tests
composer.json
composer.lock
phpunit.xml
phpunit-integration.xml
.phpunit.cache
